    4. For each sprite, add 1-12 noise pixels (11-33% of clean count).
       Each noise pixel must be 4-adjacent to a clean pixel, its mirror across
       the axis must be bg, and it must not pair with another noise pixel.
    5. Verify best-axis score gap >= 2 over 2nd-best for the noisy shape.
       Reject and re-add noise if violated.
    6. The input is the noisy grid; the output is the clean grid.
